  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 957101,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 100,000 Pyramid (Commodore 64) - Synopsis\n\nStep into the fast-paced world of the classic TV game show with *100,000 Pyramid* for the Commodore 64! This early adaptation faithfully recreates the thrilling challenge of reaching the pyramid's peak. Two players face off in successive rounds, choosing categories filled with interconnected words – think \"things that are red\" or \"types of vehicles.\"\n\nThe core gameplay revolves around clever clue-giving. One player acts as the \"cluer,\" providing hints to their opponent who must guess the hidden words without uttering them directly. Strategic thinking and quick reflexes are key to success!  A single-player mode offers a different, less traditional experience, tasking you with crafting single-word clues to solve puzzles. \n\nExperience the tension and excitement of the original show, now in vibrant 8-bit glory.  Can you outsmart your opponent and climb to the top of the pyramid, claiming victory and the coveted title of Pyramid champion? Test your vocabulary and deduction skills in this addictive and engaging game!"
    },
